    <bf:summary>
      <bf:Summary>
	<rdfs:label>"Cities are our future and increasingly determine global resource use. Growing urbanization presents some of the most significant opportunities and challenges of our time. Today, cities suffer from severe congestion, public space is lost to car traffic and parking, and biocapacity is overspent by consumption levels and urban growth. The climate crisis highlights the need for urban policies that provide a holistic framework for sustainability, including renewable energies, highly efficient buildings, sustainable industrial and urban infrastructure and transportation"-- Provided by publisher.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:Summary>
    </bf:summary>
    <bf:tableOfContents>
      <bf:TableOfContents>
	<rdfs:label>Volume 1. Design, arts, culture and community -- Built and natural environment -- Mobile, secure and sharing cities -- Volume 4. Pathways to urban transformation.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:TableOfContents>
    </bf:tableOfContents>
